# Playwright Web Automation Standards

- Use Page Object Model: keep selectors and UI actions in `web_automation/pages/`, not in test files.
- Keep test names traceable to testcase IDs when available (for example `test_tc_001_*`).
- Prefer robust selectors in this order:
  1) `get_by_test_id`
  2) `get_by_role` with stable accessible name
  3) stable CSS locator
- Avoid brittle selectors (`nth-child`, deep XPath) unless no alternative exists.
- Use explicit assertions (`expect(...)` / clear `assert`) for user-visible behavior.
- Reuse helper methods for repeated actions (open page, login, search, navigation).
- Keep one behavior focus per test case.

## Quick Examples

```python
# ✅ Good: page object usage
novel_home = NovelHomePage(page)
novel_home.open()
novel_home.search("test")
```

```python
# ❌ Avoid: raw selectors repeated in tests
page.locator("div > ul > li:nth-child(3) > a").click()
```
